body: |-
  ## TCs verified
  - TC1 PASS: migration notice fires for cohort C (with YAML-list aspect format)
  - TC2 PASS: marker file honored, no re-fire on second invocation
  - TC3 (correctly suppressed): 0 components edge case suppresses aspect-coverage line per spec
  - TC5 PASS: shift --no-prompt writes skip marker, does NOT add compliance to roster
  - TC6 PASS: --force clears skip marker (--no-prompt order question minor)
  - TC7 PASS: writeArchetypeDefaults schema matches spec §2 byte-exact (3 claims, severity advise, source archetype-default)
  - TC8 PASS: cohort A (compliance rostered) — no notice, no marker file

  ## Bug detail
  - File: packages/paradigm/src/core/migration-notices.ts:60
  - Original: `if (/^\s*~/m.test(content)) return true;`
  - Fixed:    `if (/^\s*-?\s*~/m.test(content)) return true;`
  - New regex matches both `~aspect:` (mapping key) AND `- ~aspect` (YAML list item)
  - Test file: src/core/migration-notices.test.ts +1 test ("detects YAML-list aspect form (- ~name) — the standard .purpose shape")

  ## Why unit tests missed it
  Existing isCohortC tests used `~something:` and `~thing:` (mapping-key form) — the only form the original regex matched. The standard .purpose shape across this repo's 100+ .purpose files is the YAML-list form (`aspects:\n      - ~name`), but the unit tests never exercised that form.

  ## Why the smoke test caught it
  Used a realistic .purpose seed format mirroring this repo's actual conventions. Doctor's first invocation showed no migration notice → marker file missing → predicate failure → debug pointed to regex.

  ## Cost / save
  Smoke test cost ~10 min wall clock + 1 round-trip on the regex fix + re-test. Caught a bug that would have shipped to npm and silently broken cohort-C migration for users of the canonical YAML-list .purpose format. v5.21.1-v5.21.4 history shows what happens without this gate (3 patches for what should have been 1).
